the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    *a set* is a subset of *a set*.
    the concatenation of *a list* then *a list* is *a list*.
    *a thing* followed by is *a second thing* with *a third thing*.
    *a thing* is a set; scenario element.
    *a thing* belongs to *a set*; scenario element.
    *a thing* has as head before *a second thing* with *a third thing*.

the knowledge base list includes:

the text of the source program is at "sources/list-scasp.pl".

a set is a subset of a second set if
    the set is a set
    and the second set is a set
    and for all cases in which
        a thing belongs to the set
        it is the case that
            the thing belongs to the second set.

the concatenation of [] then a list is the list.

